WEBVTT

00:01.210 --> 00:04.674
<i>♪ it seems today
 that all you see ♪</i>

00:04.760 --> 00:07.723
<i>♪ is violence in movies
 and sex on tv ♪</i>

00:07.892 --> 00:11.648
<i>♪ but where are those
 good old-fashioned values ♪</i>

00:11.734 --> 00:14.655
<i>♪ on which we used to rely? ♪</i>

00:14.741 --> 00:18.079
<i>♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪</i>

00:18.166 --> 00:21.296
<i>♪ lucky there's a man who
 positively can do ♪</i>

00:21.423 --> 00:23.008
<i>♪ all the things that make us ♪</i>

00:23.093 --> 00:24.260
<i>♪ laugh and cry ♪</i>

00:24.388 --> 00:30.232
<i>♪ he's... A...
 Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪</i>

00:34.828 --> 00:37.499
Thanks for bringing us
to your company picnic, peter.

00:37.584 --> 00:39.337
This is gonna be so much fun.

00:39.422 --> 00:41.717
Yeah, I figured it's
finally time you guys put faces

00:41.761 --> 00:44.139
To the people I've been bitching
about for the past eight years.

00:44.225 --> 00:46.436
Oop, there's charity 5k guy.

00:46.522 --> 00:49.150
Let's run lupus
out of town, huh, guys?

00:50.864 --> 00:52.407
I work with peter now.

00:52.493 --> 00:55.289
There's the guy who started
after me, and was beneath me,

00:55.333 --> 00:57.293
But now he's, like,
higher up than I am.

00:57.338 --> 00:59.800
-Hey, bob.
-Hey, darren.

01:02.641 --> 01:05.103
Thank you all for coming
to today's picnic.

01:05.147 --> 01:08.235
Now, for our main event:
The aerial ovum transfer,

01:08.321 --> 01:11.325
Or, as it's sometimes known,
the egg toss.

01:11.452 --> 01:13.414
This year, as a special prize,

01:13.499 --> 01:15.627
The winning team
will receive a five-night stay

01:15.754 --> 01:18.634
At my vacation home
in mooseattackee, maine.

01:18.761 --> 01:20.680
With miles of trails,
it is one of maine's

01:20.807 --> 01:22.643
Premiere hiking destinations.

01:22.770 --> 01:24.899
And you're only
a short bike ride away

01:24.984 --> 01:26.652
From its quaint downtown.

01:26.738 --> 01:31.163
Let your cares melt away as you
paddle across serene lake June.

01:31.248 --> 01:33.125
Peter, that place
in maine is amazing.

01:33.211 --> 01:34.962
It looks
like a stephen king book

01:35.090 --> 01:36.884
Before anything bad happens.

01:37.011 --> 01:39.223
Hi, gary, how's it going?
How's brenda?

01:39.350 --> 01:42.230
Oh, she's great.
Uh, just alive, super alive.

01:42.273 --> 01:44.735
-How are the boys?
-Yep, all alive.

01:44.862 --> 01:46.447
Children and pets all alive

01:46.574 --> 01:48.953
And acting
like normal children and pets.

01:49.038 --> 01:51.375
That's great.
H-hey, have you met

01:51.503 --> 01:53.505
That new stranger from not here?

01:53.590 --> 01:56.553
Nope.
See you tomorrow definitely.

01:59.604 --> 02:01.231
Peter,
we got to win this vacation,

02:01.400 --> 02:03.110
But there are
so many other teams.

02:03.237 --> 02:05.365
Relax, lois.
I brought a hard-boiled egg,

02:05.450 --> 02:07.620
So while all the other teams
are getting eliminated,

02:07.706 --> 02:09.834
We can just play
an "angry dad" game of catch.

02:09.961 --> 02:12.799
So the school called to say
they found pot in your locker.

02:12.884 --> 02:14.428
You want to tell me about that?

02:14.513 --> 02:17.350
Ow! I-I'm not sure
what we're doing, peter.

02:17.395 --> 02:19.689
So how's that summer job hunt
coming?

02:19.859 --> 02:22.738
I don't think they're hiring
in front of the tv all day.

02:22.865 --> 02:25.244
Ow! That's too hard.

02:25.330 --> 02:26.663
You know what else is hard?

02:26.790 --> 02:28.877
Waking up next to a woman
you no longer love.

02:28.962 --> 02:30.422
Try that on for size.

02:31.761 --> 02:34.222
[indistinct chatter]

02:34.308 --> 02:36.269
Peter, they've all
been eliminated.

02:36.355 --> 02:39.067
The game is over,
but I think we should talk.

02:39.152 --> 02:41.948
Yes! The griffins
are going to maine.

02:42.034 --> 02:43.911
And if that isn't
the perfect promo

02:44.081 --> 02:46.416
For the middle of a meaningless
vikings-packers game,

02:46.503 --> 02:47.920
I don't know what is.

02:48.048 --> 02:51.345
<i> Announcer: And the players
 have gathered around clark.</i>

02:51.472 --> 02:54.727
<i> And we can only hope that
 his injury wasn't too serious</i>

02:54.854 --> 02:58.444
<i> And we start to see some
 movement in those extremities.</i>

02:58.571 --> 03:01.535
<i> And while we have
 this break in the action,</i>

03:01.662 --> 03:04.374
<i> This Sunday
 on an all-new family guy,</i>

03:04.459 --> 03:07.423
<i>The griffins are going to maine.</i>

03:07.508 --> 03:11.683
<i> On right after
 an all-new bob's burgers.</i>

03:14.482 --> 03:16.777
A family vacation in maine.

03:16.863 --> 03:20.160
My monogrammed canvas bag
is gonna be so excited.

03:20.288 --> 03:22.039
You said it, lois.

03:22.125 --> 03:24.336
I can't wait to get stuffed
with old sunscreens

03:24.422 --> 03:26.340
And emergency tampons.

03:26.426 --> 03:28.345
Yo, a pool table?

03:28.431 --> 03:31.227
Hell ya! I'm gonna be
gettin' all up in that.

03:31.354 --> 03:34.610
How does one get
"all up in" a pool table?

03:34.737 --> 03:36.740
And, wow, look,
it's bigger than I thought.

03:36.825 --> 03:38.159
So many bedrooms.

03:38.287 --> 03:39.204
Yeah, with all that extra space,

03:39.331 --> 03:40.498
We could invite
our friends along.

03:40.709 --> 03:43.254
Quagmire, joe and bonnie,
cleveland and his family.

03:43.381 --> 03:45.133
-The whole gang could come.
-Really?

03:45.219 --> 03:47.347
Do you think
everyone would enjoy it?

03:47.432 --> 03:49.268
Lois, do you know
what's up in maine?

03:49.312 --> 03:50.771
Art's trading post.

03:50.857 --> 03:52.484
Ever since I was a kid,
I wanted to go up there

03:52.569 --> 03:53.946
To see the trained bear show.

03:53.989 --> 03:56.200
They ride bikes,
they wear dracula fangs--

03:56.286 --> 03:57.955
Seasonally--
and then there's one part

03:58.082 --> 04:00.544
Where nipsy the brown bear
pretends to smoke a cigar.

04:00.629 --> 04:02.381
And I'm not even kidding.

04:02.508 --> 04:03.759
Ah, I don't know, peter.

04:03.886 --> 04:05.764
It's a lot of people
under one roof.

04:05.849 --> 04:07.977
Come on, lois,
this is our big chance

04:08.063 --> 04:09.898
To yell at kids who aren't ours.

04:09.984 --> 04:11.402
You know what? Let's do it.

04:11.529 --> 04:13.114
I think bonnie's gained
five pounds,

04:13.283 --> 04:14.742
And I want to see her
in a swimsuit.

04:14.828 --> 04:17.541
While we're on the subject
of mrs. Swanson and swimsuits,

04:17.626 --> 04:19.879
Question:
If mrs. Swanson goes swimming,

04:19.965 --> 04:22.134
Then hangs her bathing suit
to dry in the bathroom,

04:22.262 --> 04:24.389
Am I allowed to wring
the water into a cup?

04:24.474 --> 04:26.101
-And do what with it?
-Irrelevant.

04:26.187 --> 04:28.315
Do not concern yourself
with what happens to the water

04:28.400 --> 04:31.113
Once it's in the cup.
Am I allowed?

04:31.198 --> 04:33.201
Uh, I'm gonna say no.

04:33.287 --> 04:35.999
All right, well, the guy
from reddit already paid

04:36.084 --> 04:37.920
For the water, but I'll--

04:38.048 --> 04:40.050
I'll figure something out.

04:53.123 --> 04:56.003
I've been waiting a long time
for this trip, brian.

04:56.089 --> 04:57.590
To come to maine? Huh.

04:57.676 --> 04:59.302
I didn't think you were much
of an outdoorsman.

04:59.429 --> 05:01.014
[scoffs] the outdoors
can get stuffed.

05:01.183 --> 05:02.559
We're near kennebunkport,

05:02.687 --> 05:04.438
Home of the bush family compound

05:04.565 --> 05:06.443
<i>And,
according to dowdy magazine,</i>

05:06.529 --> 05:08.573
The very place
where barbara bush picked

05:08.659 --> 05:10.411
That one haircut 40 years ago

05:10.496 --> 05:12.457
And never looked back. See?

05:12.501 --> 05:14.838
The perfect, coiffed, lady fro.

05:14.923 --> 05:17.218
I hear tell that she brought
a quaker oats box

05:17.262 --> 05:19.472
Into the salon and said, "this."

05:19.559 --> 05:22.187
Uh-oh, no pavement,
lot of rocks and roots.

05:22.273 --> 05:24.526
Good thing joe brought his

05:24.653 --> 05:26.488
New off-road tires!

05:26.616 --> 05:28.535
I didn't pack the tires.

05:28.704 --> 05:30.582
Oh.

05:30.709 --> 05:32.252
Nuts.

05:32.421 --> 05:34.089
All right, gang,
time to head inside.

05:34.175 --> 05:35.426
Now one quick heads-up.

05:35.553 --> 05:37.556
Every room has a lake view
except one.

05:37.641 --> 05:38.767
Somebody's gonna have
to look out

05:38.894 --> 05:41.272
Over that girls' volleyball camp
next door.

05:41.399 --> 05:44.154
Nice serve, stacy.

05:49.460 --> 05:50.920
What did I tell ya, lois?

05:51.005 --> 05:52.840
Look at
all those big smiles and--

05:52.967 --> 05:56.516
Cleveland jr., no wet feet
on the hardwood floor!

05:56.643 --> 05:58.478
This is gonna be a great week.

05:58.563 --> 06:00.399
Hey, peter,
will you call your boss?

06:00.527 --> 06:02.655
For what? I don't want
to bug him already.

06:02.740 --> 06:04.659
He wrote the wi-fi password
in a font

06:04.744 --> 06:07.874
Where the big letter I's and the
l juniors are the same thing.

06:07.960 --> 06:10.004
I can't make
heads or tails of it.

06:10.090 --> 06:12.552
Are you calling preston?
Ask him about the towel sitch.

06:12.637 --> 06:14.807
I could only find three
and you're gonna need those

06:14.934 --> 06:16.895
To clean the soda off
the pool table.

06:16.981 --> 06:19.359
We already spilled
on the pool table?

06:19.444 --> 06:21.948
Yeah, meg was really
gettin' all up in it.

06:22.033 --> 06:24.746
Hey, peter? Uh, someone
either laid a giant turd

06:24.832 --> 06:27.168
Or tried to flush
a russet potato down the toilet.

06:27.296 --> 06:28.881
It's totally clogged.

06:31.430 --> 06:34.895
<i> Announcer:
 And clark, still unresponsive,</i>

06:35.022 --> 06:39.572
<i> Being carted off the field
 and into an ambulance.</i>

06:39.657 --> 06:44.541
<i> This week's family guy:
 Someone lays a giant turd.</i>

06:50.181 --> 06:53.561
It's the single largest
defecate I ever saw.

06:53.647 --> 06:56.318
Should we try flushing it
again as a show of force?

06:56.487 --> 06:58.990
Nah, chris,
that'll only make it angry.

06:59.159 --> 07:01.580
Okay, here's the situation:
A stubborn bm

07:01.666 --> 07:03.376
Is blocking up our main toilet.

07:03.503 --> 07:05.506
I can't find a plunger,
so whoever did it

07:05.591 --> 07:07.385
Needs to get in there
with a dishwashing glove

07:07.470 --> 07:09.515
And punch it through.
So who was it?

07:11.604 --> 07:14.776
Say, chris, that looks like a
fresh rim of sweat on your hat.

07:14.862 --> 07:17.031
Wouldn't happen to be
"pushing sweat," would it?

07:17.158 --> 07:19.871
What? No!
I was reading a chapter book.

07:19.957 --> 07:22.127
Meg, you're generally gross.

07:22.212 --> 07:23.797
Anything you want to fess up to?

07:23.882 --> 07:26.712
Nope. I'm "dogging it"
this month for the environment.

07:26.806 --> 07:28.641
That means I only go outside.

07:28.727 --> 07:29.936
Saves water, feeds the soil,

07:29.980 --> 07:32.233
Turns a few heads
at the same time.

07:32.318 --> 07:33.945
Okay, this is disgusting.

07:34.072 --> 07:35.657
D-does it really matter
who did it?

07:35.784 --> 07:37.411
I'd kind of like to know.

07:37.496 --> 07:39.458
Yeah, we should
at least make sure

07:39.543 --> 07:41.045
They don't need
medical attention.

07:41.213 --> 07:43.175
Well, I'd like to get on
with my vacation.

07:43.302 --> 07:45.387
There's got to be a plunger
around here somewhere.

07:45.474 --> 07:46.891
Peter, come on, help me look.

07:46.976 --> 07:49.397
Okay, listen up,
we don't have much time.

07:49.483 --> 07:51.485
It was me, peter.
I clogged the toilet.

07:51.570 --> 07:54.074
That was you?
How is that even possible?

07:54.202 --> 07:56.663
[groans] it was all
that fiber-y mom cereal

07:56.749 --> 07:58.084
<i> The view told us to eat.</i>

07:58.211 --> 08:00.964
That turd has joy behar's
fingerprints all over it.

08:01.050 --> 08:03.629
But I need you
to take the fall for me.

08:03.765 --> 08:05.266
Uh, I don't know, lois.

08:05.393 --> 08:07.145
Even for a husky guy like me,

08:07.231 --> 08:08.524
It's shamefully large.

08:08.692 --> 08:10.862
I know!
That's why I need your help.

08:10.948 --> 08:12.951
That is not a poop
a woman can come back from.

08:13.036 --> 08:14.871
Look, you take the blame,
and I'll let you

08:14.915 --> 08:17.043
Get two souvenirs
at the bear show.

08:17.129 --> 08:19.549
It's not gonna be, like,
like, like, books, is it?

08:19.634 --> 08:20.844
No.

08:20.929 --> 08:22.722
All right, everybody, listen up.

08:22.766 --> 08:24.769
I'm the one
who clogged the toilet.

08:24.813 --> 08:26.690
[all clamoring in disgust]

08:26.775 --> 08:29.279
Oh, great! As if that
little slug of yours

08:29.364 --> 08:30.699
Isn't embarrassing enough.

08:30.826 --> 08:32.871
Sorry, I have
to make this believable.

08:33.039 --> 08:34.749
-So it's big?
-Let's...

08:34.877 --> 08:37.882
Let's just
get through this, huh?

08:42.394 --> 08:44.856
<i>[to the tune of "reveille"]
♪ gig-gig-giggity ♪</i>

08:44.983 --> 08:46.861
<i>♪ gig-gig-giggity, gig-gig,
 giggity, gee-gee ♪</i>

08:46.946 --> 08:48.823
<i>♪ gig-gig-giggity
 gig-gig-giggity, gee-gee. ♪</i>

08:48.909 --> 08:50.953
What the hell is happening?!

08:51.039 --> 08:52.832
Life, peter.
That's what's happening.

08:52.959 --> 08:54.921
I've put together
a whole itinerary of adventures

08:54.964 --> 08:57.676
-For our week.
-Wow, this is very detailed.

08:57.804 --> 09:01.268
"6:27, read '6:27'
on daily schedule."

09:01.395 --> 09:02.813
Right on schedule.

09:02.899 --> 09:04.860
Hey, why's some of this stuff
highlighted in green,

09:04.987 --> 09:06.739
But my bear show is in yellow?

09:06.824 --> 09:08.493
Because the bear show
is priority yellow.

09:08.578 --> 09:11.625
[laughing] a bear, a bear show
would never be priority green.

09:11.752 --> 09:14.173
All right, as long
as it's on there, I guess.

09:14.259 --> 09:16.637
Now to put on a pair of shorts
I never wear at home,

09:16.764 --> 09:19.936
But packed for vacation,
hoping they'd magically fit.

09:23.404 --> 09:25.407
[grunting]

09:28.499 --> 09:30.042
[sighs]

09:30.169 --> 09:31.796
<i> Announcer:
 Vacation: Let's just pack</i>

09:31.881 --> 09:33.675
<i> The stuff we're sure fits.</i>

09:33.803 --> 09:35.471
[inhales deeply]

09:35.598 --> 09:37.183
[exhales]

09:37.227 --> 09:38.394
You guys smell that?

09:38.479 --> 09:39.731
You smell that air?

09:39.858 --> 09:42.529
[all inhale, exhale]

09:42.689 --> 09:44.450
Peter, you still back there?

09:44.535 --> 09:45.953
I don't hear you
smelling that air.

09:46.039 --> 09:48.042
[panting]
yeah, I'm here.

09:48.127 --> 09:50.046
I'm just having a hard time
on the one bike

09:50.214 --> 09:51.967
That was stored
under the deck all winter

09:52.053 --> 09:54.473
Instead of in the garage.
[sighs]

09:54.558 --> 09:56.143
We've been at this all morning.

09:56.270 --> 09:57.855
Is it time to go
to the bear show yet?

09:58.024 --> 09:59.650
Soon, peter. But before that,

09:59.779 --> 10:02.950
The itinerary has us going
to a must-visit local market

10:03.119 --> 10:05.831
That no local
has ever stepped foot in.

10:07.797 --> 10:09.465
Now, be sure to put
your bikes down in a place

10:09.592 --> 10:12.806
That blocks the path of people
just trying to live their lives.

10:14.395 --> 10:15.938
[crowd clamoring]

10:16.023 --> 10:18.945
We're doing vacation
really good, you guys.

10:18.988 --> 10:21.075
God, I hate these stores.

10:21.160 --> 10:22.870
They're so tiny, so the owner's

10:22.914 --> 10:24.541
Right on top of you
the whole time.

10:24.626 --> 10:26.421
-Can I wrap that for you?
-Hoda kotb!

10:26.548 --> 10:28.926
Oh, you're such a tourist.
Here, follow my lead.

10:29.011 --> 10:31.098
You know how it's
typically rude to talk

10:31.258 --> 10:33.352
-To people about their finances?
-Yeah.

10:33.439 --> 10:35.774
Well, in a small town market,
you can come right out

10:35.902 --> 10:38.489
And ask the owner if he makes
enough money to feed his family.

10:38.575 --> 10:40.870
You just have to do it
in the voice white ladies use

10:41.038 --> 10:43.167
With people
who don't speak english.

10:43.252 --> 10:45.755
Was it a good tourist season,

10:45.924 --> 10:48.178
Or will your children
go without?

10:48.263 --> 10:50.726
This business you've
dedicated your life to

10:50.853 --> 10:52.646
Is very cute to me.

10:52.815 --> 10:54.609
Isn't this fun, peter?

10:54.695 --> 10:57.783
Now don't forget to say "bye"
like the world's biggest ass.

10:57.911 --> 11:02.251
[high-pitched]
bye! Buh-bye, bye.

11:02.378 --> 11:04.173
♪ ♪

11:05.177 --> 11:07.222
How are those burgers
coming along?

11:07.307 --> 11:08.349
Fine, I guess.

11:08.434 --> 11:10.771
Well, thanks for
volunteering to cook.

11:10.814 --> 11:11.899
I didn't volunteer.

11:11.984 --> 11:13.401
Everyone just
called me "grill master"

11:13.530 --> 11:14.738
Until I submitted.

11:14.823 --> 11:17.453
[laughs] spoken like
a true grill master.

11:17.580 --> 11:19.707
Whatever. Hey, everybody,
we got to eat quick

11:19.794 --> 11:21.587
If we're gonna
catch the bear show.

11:21.673 --> 11:24.093
They're kept on a robitussin
and zoloft-heavy diet,

11:24.178 --> 11:25.805
So they fall asleep
pretty early.

11:25.890 --> 11:28.520
Okay, I'll tell chris.
He's down at the dock fishing.

11:28.647 --> 11:31.192
There he is, the bait master.

11:31.319 --> 11:34.533
I think I misunderstood
the assignment.

11:34.618 --> 11:36.120
Well, let's see what you caught.

11:36.205 --> 11:38.585
I wouldn't look in the bucket.

11:43.138 --> 11:45.809
I'm sorry,
we closed 20 minutes ago.

11:45.894 --> 11:47.980
What? Wait a minute,
if you closed 20 minutes ago,

11:48.108 --> 11:49.735
Why are you just
flipping the sign now?

11:49.862 --> 11:51.280
Owner said
I had to wait to flip it

11:51.407 --> 11:52.992
Until it would
devastate a fat guy.

11:53.119 --> 11:55.874
I told him he was crazy,
but you look pretty upset.

11:56.001 --> 11:57.502
That's why he's the boss.

11:57.588 --> 11:58.963
What's going on, peter?

11:59.050 --> 12:00.635
They're closed,
that's what's going on.

12:00.720 --> 12:02.889
And now we got to come
all the way back here tomorrow.

12:03.017 --> 12:04.644
Oh, we're actually
closed permanently.

12:04.771 --> 12:07.608
After decades of very valid
animal cruelty complaints,

12:07.736 --> 12:09.363
It was easier to
shut down than to

12:09.448 --> 12:11.576
Keep cleaning fake peta blood
off our clothes.

12:11.662 --> 12:12.703
I'm sorry, what?

12:12.789 --> 12:14.415
Yeah, honestly, it's a miracle

12:14.542 --> 12:16.002
They let us go
as long as we did.

12:16.088 --> 12:18.383
There's not a single license
or permit for this whole thing.

12:18.510 --> 12:21.974
One day, we just started
putting bears on pogo sticks

12:22.060 --> 12:23.603
And no one ever told us to stop.

12:23.772 --> 12:25.023
This can't be happening.

12:25.067 --> 12:27.194
Sorry, you should've
been here earlier

12:27.238 --> 12:29.199
For the bear flash sale.
I was strapping 'em to

12:29.284 --> 12:31.329
People's cars
like christmas trees.

12:31.456 --> 12:33.041
See, that guy got one.

12:34.964 --> 12:37.008
By the end,
we didn't even charge people.

12:37.136 --> 12:39.180
We were just
giving the bears away.

12:39.266 --> 12:40.767
<i>[echoing]
 just giving the bears away.</i>

12:40.853 --> 12:43.606
<i> Just giving the bears away.
 Just giving the bears away.</i>

12:45.405 --> 12:47.700
Sorry you didn't
see the bears, peter,

12:47.827 --> 12:50.706
But quagmire has us going
blueberry-picking tomorrow.

12:50.834 --> 12:52.084
Maybe you'll see a bear then.

12:52.170 --> 12:54.298
I do not want to
see a wild bear, lois.

12:54.425 --> 12:56.428
I want to see
a unicycle bear in a fez.

12:56.513 --> 12:58.390
You know,
I still don't really get it.

12:58.517 --> 12:59.977
A bear on a unicycle?

13:00.104 --> 13:01.189
It sounds kind of dumb.

13:01.316 --> 13:03.318
It's not dumb. It's hilarious

13:03.446 --> 13:05.866
And it's the only thing
I wanted to do this entire trip.

13:05.993 --> 13:07.411
You know,
if I remember correctly,

13:07.580 --> 13:09.290
Part of our deal was
I get two souvenirs

13:09.417 --> 13:11.212
From the bear show.
Well, I'm looking around

13:11.339 --> 13:14.009
And I don't see
any plastic bear heads on sticks

13:14.094 --> 13:15.346
That I can make bite things.

13:15.431 --> 13:17.768
That means I get to
tell everyone it was you

13:17.812 --> 13:18.812
Who clogged the toilet.

13:18.939 --> 13:20.148
[all gasp]

13:20.275 --> 13:22.237
Lois, that was you?

13:22.322 --> 13:24.324
But it had such a man stink.

13:24.451 --> 13:25.953
You know what, donna?
Going in the bathroom after you

13:26.038 --> 13:27.874
Ain't exactly a walk
through the rose garden,

13:27.960 --> 13:29.126
So I'd be quiet right about now.

13:29.212 --> 13:30.505
Don't listen to him, donna.

13:30.590 --> 13:33.220
We think your movements smell
very lady-like.

13:33.305 --> 13:34.597
Isn't that right, kids?

13:34.683 --> 13:36.811
Oh, of course, 'cause
you all agree on everything.

13:36.980 --> 13:39.066
Just the perfect family,
aren't you?

13:39.151 --> 13:41.113
News flash:
Normal families fight

13:41.198 --> 13:43.158
And like spending time
away from each other.

13:43.202 --> 13:46.249
Sir? Sir? I'm gonna need you
to calm down, sir.

13:46.376 --> 13:48.129
Stop acting like
a real cop, joe.

13:48.256 --> 13:49.464
Your right leg is in a knot.

13:49.592 --> 13:51.010
Uh, yeah,

13:51.137 --> 13:52.054
They got a little tangled

13:52.181 --> 13:53.307
When bonnie dipped me

13:53.392 --> 13:54.685
In the lake.

13:54.770 --> 13:57.107
God, I can't believe I thought
it'd be a good idea

13:57.234 --> 13:58.402
To bring you people
on this trip.

13:58.487 --> 14:00.489
The only reason I still
talk to any of you

14:00.617 --> 14:01.910
Is 'cause
we live on the same street.

14:02.120 --> 14:05.167
And after this week, I am
seriously considering a move.

14:05.252 --> 14:08.257
Peter, peter. I'm sorry,
but 7:05 sunset,

14:08.343 --> 14:10.429
So I need to simulate more
trumpet songs with "giggity."

14:10.514 --> 14:13.728
<i>[to the tune of "taps"]
♪ giggity ♪</i>

14:13.813 --> 14:16.108
<i>♪ giggity. ♪</i>

14:16.194 --> 14:17.403
Give me that thing.

14:17.447 --> 14:19.199
Oh, no.
How will you distract yourself

14:19.284 --> 14:21.120
From the fact that
you're gonna die alone

14:21.206 --> 14:22.749
Without your precious itinerary?

14:22.876 --> 14:24.378
-Whoa.
-Aah! Son of a--

14:24.463 --> 14:25.546
[gasps]

14:28.472 --> 14:29.472
[all gasp]

14:31.186 --> 14:33.439
[panicked shouting]

14:34.736 --> 14:35.778
[clamoring]

14:38.453 --> 14:40.497
Oh, my god. The cabin's on fire.

14:40.582 --> 14:41.625
Heavens.

14:48.685 --> 14:50.896
Hey, thanks for coming out.
Guess all that's left to do

14:50.982 --> 14:52.315
Is get a picture of me
in the truck

14:52.444 --> 14:54.571
And, uh, you fellas
can be on your way.

14:56.201 --> 14:57.619
Oh, god, look at this place.

14:57.788 --> 14:59.833
If preston finds out
I torched his house,

14:59.918 --> 15:00.960
I'm screwed, you guys.

15:01.046 --> 15:02.673
We got to fix this fast.

15:03.752 --> 15:05.345
But I'm sure it's nothing

15:05.473 --> 15:07.893
A resourceful group of
best friends like us

15:08.020 --> 15:08.895
Can't handle, right?

15:09.023 --> 15:10.691
♪ ♪

15:12.990 --> 15:15.786
Look, I know peter said
some very mean things,

15:15.829 --> 15:18.751
But what's important right now
is that no one was hurt.

15:18.836 --> 15:20.630
That's not entirely true, lois.

15:20.716 --> 15:23.888
Your reusable grocery bags
didn't make it.

15:23.932 --> 15:25.349
[scoffs] what?

15:25.435 --> 15:28.347
Your bags, they were
lost in the fire.

15:28.483 --> 15:30.319
No. No.

15:30.446 --> 15:31.488
No!

15:31.573 --> 15:32.991
[grunts]

15:33.077 --> 15:33.952
-[clamoring]
-you son of a bitch,

15:34.122 --> 15:35.122
Peter griffin!

15:35.207 --> 15:37.084
What have you done?

15:37.212 --> 15:38.671
I will never
forgive you for this.

15:38.757 --> 15:40.007
Do you hear me?

15:40.093 --> 15:43.599
[sobbing]
I will never forgive you.

15:44.854 --> 15:46.898
♪ ♪

15:49.114 --> 15:51.283
Well, peter,
you made it crystal clear

15:51.369 --> 15:54.415
We're no longer wanted,
so we'll leave you be.

15:54.585 --> 15:56.253
Yeah, you can deal with
this mess on your own.

15:56.380 --> 15:58.215
Let's go, everybody.

16:01.224 --> 16:03.186
[car doors closing]

16:03.313 --> 16:05.148
[engines starting]

16:05.266 --> 16:06.318
Why aren't we moving?

16:06.403 --> 16:07.778
We got to wait for joe

16:07.865 --> 16:09.032
To back out of the driveway

16:09.117 --> 16:10.619
'cause he pulled in last.

16:10.662 --> 16:13.542
Sorry. If I knew you were doing
a big, dramatic exit,

16:13.628 --> 16:16.340
I would've rearranged the cars
this morning.

16:16.425 --> 16:19.180
You mind if I wait till I'm
all the way in to tell you off?

16:19.265 --> 16:21.393
Yeah, that's fine.

16:27.785 --> 16:29.829
Shame on you, peter.

16:29.957 --> 16:31.040
It is people like you who--

16:31.125 --> 16:32.084
[car horn honking]

16:32.212 --> 16:33.212
[quagmire]
go!

16:33.297 --> 16:35.467
♪ ♪

16:36.973 --> 16:38.348
All right, peter, don't panic.

16:38.434 --> 16:39.768
You got till the end of
the week to fix this.

16:39.853 --> 16:43.025
Maybe there's an online
tutorial that'll help.

16:43.111 --> 16:44.445
<i> What's going on, guys?</i>

16:44.531 --> 16:46.575
<i>I'm corey, from "corey's world."</i>

16:46.661 --> 16:48.579
<i> Today I'm gonna show you
 how to patch a big hole</i>

16:48.666 --> 16:51.253
<i> In your boss's cabin.
 Here's what you'll need:</i>

16:51.338 --> 16:53.508
<i>[fading]
 a drywall saw, tape measure...</i>

16:53.593 --> 16:54.552
[peter]
shoot, what did he say?

16:54.637 --> 16:56.264
<i>Turn off the power so you don't</i>

16:56.349 --> 16:59.062
<i> Drill into a live wire
 like my stepdad todd.</i>

16:59.148 --> 17:00.399
<i> Now our spoons move</i>

17:00.484 --> 17:01.484
<i> When he walks in the kitchen.</i>

17:01.570 --> 17:02.486
<i> To do that...</i>

17:02.572 --> 17:04.575
[peter]
gerbils can't sing opera.

17:04.702 --> 17:05.911
Damn it, peter, focus.

17:05.997 --> 17:07.372
-Your job is on the lin--
-[mouse button clicks]

17:07.459 --> 17:10.338
[singing "o sole mio"]

17:13.597 --> 17:16.810
[laughs] aw, touché,
"recommended videos."

17:16.897 --> 17:18.648
I know you're leading me
down a rabbit hole

17:18.734 --> 17:21.739
To isis beheadings,
but this was a bull's-eye.

17:21.866 --> 17:23.493
[phone rings]

17:23.661 --> 17:25.748
Preston. I wasn't
expecting to hear from you

17:25.875 --> 17:26.750
For a couple of days.

17:26.877 --> 17:28.462
Yes, well, I realized

17:28.547 --> 17:31.010
I only provided three towels
for the entire cabin,

17:31.137 --> 17:33.223
So I'm on my way
to deliver more.

17:33.308 --> 17:35.896
Oh, you don't have to come all
the way up here just for that.

17:35.981 --> 17:37.358
Unfortunately, I do.

17:37.443 --> 17:40.197
My ocd won't allow me to stop...
[clicks tongue] clicking

17:40.324 --> 17:42.452
Until the cabin has 15 towels.

17:42.496 --> 17:43.997
Well, I should let you go.

17:44.083 --> 17:46.503
A new car is in front of me
and I need to... [clicks tongue]

17:46.588 --> 17:49.343
Do math problems
with its license plate number.

17:49.387 --> 17:52.057
♪ ♪

17:53.604 --> 17:55.732
All right, everything I need to
get out of this mess

17:55.818 --> 17:58.196
Is right here.
Power drill, level,

17:58.240 --> 17:59.950
Circular saw. Perfect.

18:00.078 --> 18:02.289
How can preston fire me

18:02.417 --> 18:03.960
If he can't get inside?

18:04.087 --> 18:05.087
[wind gusts]

18:05.214 --> 18:06.632
Ah! My defenses are down.

18:06.718 --> 18:07.927
-[car approaching]
-oh, no.

18:08.013 --> 18:09.305
He's here. [sighs]

18:09.390 --> 18:11.685
Well, I guess it's time to
face the music.

18:15.739 --> 18:17.156
What are you guys doing here?

18:17.283 --> 18:19.036
We came back to help you, peter.

18:19.163 --> 18:20.748
And it's not just us.

18:20.833 --> 18:23.630
♪ ♪

18:27.139 --> 18:28.056
Did we time it right?

18:28.141 --> 18:29.601
Did you say "not just us"

18:29.728 --> 18:31.104
Before we pulled over
the horizon?

18:31.190 --> 18:32.558
Yeah, it was perfect.

18:32.610 --> 18:34.195
Yes. That is why we practiced

18:34.280 --> 18:35.490
In the walmart parking lot.

18:35.575 --> 18:37.577
But I was
such a jerk to all of you.

18:37.663 --> 18:38.747
Why would you help me now?

18:38.832 --> 18:40.961
Lois says you were the one
pushing to

18:41.088 --> 18:42.422
Invite us on the trip at all.

18:42.508 --> 18:43.633
Called us your best friends.

18:43.677 --> 18:44.928
And we should've
made a better effort to

18:45.013 --> 18:47.600
Get to your bear show,
instead of making the trip

18:47.686 --> 18:48.895
All about what we wanted to do.

18:49.022 --> 18:50.899
Yeah, and we left without
any of our chargers.

18:50.985 --> 18:53.573
If it was just the blocks,
you know, big whoop-dee-doo,

18:53.700 --> 18:55.368
But it was the wires, too.

18:55.453 --> 18:56.871
So, what do you say?

18:56.957 --> 18:59.085
Can we help you
fix the cabin, peter?

19:00.089 --> 19:01.131
I'd like that.

19:01.301 --> 19:02.301
Now, let's go chop down

19:02.428 --> 19:03.762
Some ancient pine trees

19:03.848 --> 19:06.268
To save this millionaire's
vacation home.

19:06.353 --> 19:07.855
[all] yeah!

19:09.485 --> 19:12.741
The chimney has proved stalwart.

19:13.620 --> 19:15.163
Well, that's preston.

19:15.290 --> 19:16.708
I'm sorry for what I said.

19:16.835 --> 19:19.548
Only true friends would come
back to help the way you did,

19:19.634 --> 19:21.260
And that's all that matters.

19:21.387 --> 19:23.307
True friends will also stay

19:23.434 --> 19:25.394
To watch their friend get fired.

19:25.521 --> 19:27.106
Thanks, guys.

19:27.150 --> 19:28.526
I'll probably cry.

19:28.612 --> 19:31.450
That's okay.
It'll make a better tiktok.

19:31.577 --> 19:32.787
Griffin, what the hell?

19:32.872 --> 19:35.209
My cabin.
It's completely destroyed.

19:35.294 --> 19:38.926
[crying] I'm so sorry, preston,

19:39.011 --> 19:41.097
But you got to know this was
completely my fault.

19:41.182 --> 19:43.477
My friends and family
were the perfect guests,

19:43.562 --> 19:44.647
And they had
nothing to do with it.

19:44.732 --> 19:46.025
If you want to fire me,

19:46.152 --> 19:47.612
Or issue some maine justice

19:47.656 --> 19:49.324
And clamp some lobsters
to my nipples,

19:49.410 --> 19:50.953
I understand.

19:53.210 --> 19:55.129
Peter, you don't understand.

19:55.214 --> 19:56.424
I hate it up here.

19:56.551 --> 19:59.004
The small-town pace,
the pressure to relax,

19:59.056 --> 20:01.769
The barn owl that pushed
my wife down a staircase.

20:01.896 --> 20:04.358
I don't get it.
Then why have the cabin at all?

20:04.485 --> 20:06.947
An address in maine
allowed me to establish

20:07.032 --> 20:10.622
An ethically dubious, but
technically legal shell company.

20:10.750 --> 20:12.334
But now,
with the money I'll save

20:12.420 --> 20:14.923
From taking a casualty deduction
on the destroyed property,

20:15.009 --> 20:16.678
I won't need that.

20:18.184 --> 20:19.977
[applause]

20:20.104 --> 20:22.483
Hey, preston,
I know the cabin's a mess,

20:22.568 --> 20:24.821
But we still got
three days in the prize week.

20:24.907 --> 20:27.620
Could we finish out our trip
here in maine? Together?

20:27.738 --> 20:29.207
I don't see why not.

20:29.292 --> 20:31.169
[bird calls]

20:35.222 --> 20:37.767
<i>[announcer]
 maine: A day and a half
 is probably enough.</i>

20:43.574 --> 20:44.825
Well, we had our troubles,

20:44.953 --> 20:47.957
But I'm glad we're back at home,
safe and sound.

20:48.043 --> 20:50.672
Peter, what are you talking
about? This is all a dream.

20:50.757 --> 20:53.512
You had a stress heart attack
during the egg toss.

20:53.597 --> 20:56.894
[groaning]

20:57.021 --> 20:59.733
Poor darren.